tal lines: 979\nL277: ## March 31, 2026\nL278: \nL279:   * Launched Veo 3.1 Lite Preview, cite65†`veo-3.1-lite-generate-preview` , our most cost-efficient cite66†video generation model, designed for rapid iteration and building high-volume applications.\nL280: \nL281:   * The `gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025` model has been shut down. Use cite67†`gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview` instead.\nL282: ## March 26, 2026\nL283: \nL284:   * Released cite68†`gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview` , the latest audio-to-audio (A2A) model designed for real-time dialogue and voice-first AI applications. Read the cite17†Live API docs to get started.\nL285: ## March 25, 2026\nL286: \nL287:   * Launched cite20†Lyria 3 music generation models: cite69†`lyria-3-clip-preview` (30-second clips) and cite70†`lyria-3-pro-preview` (full-length songs). Both models accept text and image inputs and generate high-quality, 48kHz stereo audio. See the cite20†Music generation guide for details and code samples.\nL288: \nL289: ## March 23, 2026\nL290: \nL291:   * Rolled out cite71†Prepay and Postpay billing plans in AI Studio. Existing accounts may be affected; read the cite71†Billing documentation for more information.\nL292: ## March 18, 2026\nL293: \nL294:   * Released the new cite72†Built-in Tools and Function Calling Combination feature, making it possible to use Gemini's built-in tools alongside custom function calling tools in a single API call.\nL295:   * cite73†Grounding with Google Maps is now supported for Gemini 3 models going forward.\nL296: \nL297: ## March 16, 2026\nL298: \nL299:   * Introduced revamped cite74†Usage Tiers and cite75†Billing Account spend caps for a better user billing experience.\nL300: ## March 12, 2026\nL301: \nL302:   * Introduced cite76†project-level spend caps to billing in AI Studio.\nL303: \nL304: ## March 10, 2026\nL305: \nL306:   * Released `gemini-embedding-2-preview`, our first multimodal embedding model. It supports text, image, video, audio, and PDF inputs, mapping all modalities into a unified embedding space. To learn more, see cite55†Embeddings .\nL307: \nL308:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025` model will be cite32†shut down on March 31, 2026.\nL309: ## March 9, 2026\nL310: \nL311:   * The Gemini 3 Pro Preview model has been cite32†shut down . The `gemini-3-pro-preview` now points to cite77†`gemini-3.1-pro-preview` .\nL312: \nL313: ## March 3, 2026\nL314: \nL315:   * Launched Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite Preview, the first Flash-Lite model in the Gemini 3 series. Read the cite67†model page for specs, specific updates, and developer guidance.\nL502: ## October 7, 2025\nL503: \nL504:   * Launched cite39†Gemini 2.5 Computer Use Preview L505: \nL506: ## October 2, 2025\nL507: \nL508:   * Launched Gemini 2.5 Flash Image GA: cite38†Image Generation with Gemini L509: \nL510: ## September 29, 2025\nL511: \nL512:   * The following Gemini 1.5 models are now shut down:\nL513:     * `gemini-1.5-pro`\nL514:     * `gemini-1.5-flash-8b`\nL515:     * `gemini-1.5-flash`\nL516: ## September 25, 2025\nL517: \nL518:   * Released Gemini Robotics ER 1.5 model in preview. See the cite30†Robotics overview to learn about how to use the model for your robotics application.\nL519: \nL520:   * Launched following preview models:\nL521: \nL522:     * `gemini-2.5-flash-preview-09-2025`\nL523:     * `gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025`\nL524: \nL525: See the cite93†Models page for details.\nL526: ## September 23, 2025\nL527: \nL528:   * Released `gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-09-2025`, a new native audio model for the Live API with improved function calling and speech cut off handling. To learn more, see the cite83†Live API guide and cite94†Gemini 2.5 Flash Native Audio .\nL529: ## September 16, 2025\nL530: \nL531:   * Deprecation announcement: The following models will be shut down in October 2025:\nL532: \nL533:     * `embedding-001`\nL534:     * `embedding-gecko-001`\nL535:     * `gemini-embedding-exp-03-07` (`gemini-embedding-exp`)\nL536: \nL537: See the cite55†Embeddings page for details on the latest embeddings model.\nL538: \nL539: ## September 10, 2025\nL540: \nL541:   * Released support for the cite95†Embeddings model in Batch API , and added Batch API to the cite96†OpenAI compatibility library for even easier ways to get started with batch queries.\nL542: ## September 9, 2025\nL543: \nL544:   * Launched Veo 3 and Veo 3 Fast GA, with lower pricing and new options for aspect ratios, resolution, and seeding. Read the cite97†Veo documentation for more information.\nL545: \nL546: ## August 26, 2025\nL547: \nL548:   * Launched cite98†Gemini 2.5 Image Preview , our latest native image generation model.\nL549: ## August 18, 2025\nL550: \nL551:   * Released cite99†URL context tool to general availability (GA), a tool for providing URLs as additional context to prompts. Support for using URL context with the `gemini-2.0-flash` model (available during experimental release) will be discontinued in one week.\nL552: \nL553: ## August 14, 2025\nL554: \nL555:   * Released Imagen 4 Ultra, Standard and Fast models as generally available (GA). To learn more, see the cite100†Imagen page.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNews in the Artificial Intelligence category (https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/artificial-intelligence/)\nciteturn1070view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn1069view6\",\"pattern\":\"September 23, 2026\"}); Total lines: 227\nL0: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input: Search Site]\nL1: \nL2: [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: News in the Artificial Intelligence category\nL5: \nL6:   * #### cite0†Malicious AI agents steal 600K credit cards, infect 100+ sites with skimmers L7: \nL8: A financially motivated threat actor is using open-source AI agent frameworks to attack hundreds of online retailers at scale, stealing more than 600,000 credit card records.\nL9: \nL10:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L11:     * September 23, 2026\nL12:     * 12:20 PM\nL13:     * cite2†0 L14:   * #### cite3†New ClosedQuorum Windows malware uses AI for attack decisions L15: \nL16: A new Windows malware named ClosedQuorum uses Google Gemini, DeepSeek, Qwen, and Mistral AI models to autonomously determine the actions to take during post-compromise stages of an attack.\nL17: \nL18:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L19:     * September 22, 2026\nL20:     * 02:04 PM\nL21:     * cite4†0 L22: \nL23:   * #### cite5†[Guide] How to identify risky OAuth grants and MCP server connections ^{cite6†Image†www.bleepstatic.com }\nL24: OAuth grants are the quiet back door of modern SaaS, and as the recent Klue breach showed, attackers are taking notice. This checklist gives you a repeatable way to uncover risky OAuth grants and MCP server connections before a permissive scope turns into an incident.\nL25: \nL26:     * cite5†Nudge Security Sponsorship\nL27: \nL28:   * #### cite7†New RatHat Android malware uses AI to automate device control L29: A new Android malware called RatHat has been discovered, targeting users with an AI-powered subsystem that helps operators remotely navigate compromised devices.\nL30: \nL31:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L32:     * September 17, 2026\nL33:     * 05:50 PM\nL34:     * cite8†1 L35: \nL36:   * #### cite9†OpenAI details more cases of AI agents taking unauthorized actions --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nArtificial Intelligence | Electronic Frontier Foundation (https://www.eff.org/issues/ai)\nciteturn1070view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn1069view7\",\"pattern\":\"September 23, 2026\"}); Total lines: 259\nNo matching text found for \"September 23, 2026\"-----------------------------------------------------------